# Store and check out every text file with LF endings.
#
# Inline <style>/<script> hashes in the Content-Security-Policy are computed over
# newline-normalized content, as the HTML parser does. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites the working copy to CRLF; the hashes then stop
# matching and the browser blocks every inline style and script, leaving the page
# completely unstyled. Pinning LF here keeps that from happening on any platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
